[38;5;231m⏺[39m Using [38;5;153mhyperpowers:using-hyperpowers[39m — the change ladder puts this on rung 1 (session lifetime is security posture), so
  I need a confirmation before editing.

  The change itself is one value: [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m just reads it, so nothing
  else needs touching.

  The consequence: a 16× longer session lifetime means a stolen or hijacked session token stays valid for a full working
  day instead of half an hour, and an unattended/walked-away session stays logged in all day. If sessions are
  idle-expiry (not absolute), users effectively never get logged out during a workday. That's the tradeoff — it's a real
  security posture change, not just a config value.
